# Kandelo patch rationale (S16)
# Judgment: Supported. Keep the opt-in hook because optimized Promise
# reactions otherwise discard async-context data before the bridge can
# preserve it.
#
# Node AsyncLocalStorage must retain the async context captured when a
# Promise reaction is registered. Some optimized reactions otherwise
# discard host data before the bridge can preserve it. Keep the small
# engine opt-in; the bridge already owns capture, storage and restoration.
# An OS facility cannot recover context that the engine has optimized away.
#
# Retained provisionally; see README.md: Future work: platform omissions.

# Preserve registration-time host data through the generic job-queue API.
